{
  "summary": "The experiment tested the scvi_n200 RNA encoder in a single-profile setting, achieving validation accuracy of 0.520 and F1 of 0.498, outperforming the pca_n2000 baseline (0.485 and 0.464). This suggests the RNA encoder choice may contribute to performance, though other factors could influence the difference. The impact of this encoder in single-profile settings compared to multi-profile remains uncertain, as the experiment does not isolate aggregation or fusion methods."
}

